      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village sits on the Kankakee and Minonk branch of the Illinois Central Railroad, a key line in the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://livingston.illinoisgenweb.org/flanagannebraskatwphistory.htm",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A man‑made lake called Legion Lake, originally four separate ponds, lies on the west side of Flanagan.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
